### new
cicada new <name>

create an edition-2 project

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### fix
cicada fix <score.cicada> [--all] [--check]

migrate legacy source spellings

Flags:
  --all       migrate every edition-1 score under the project folder together
  --check     report required source or manifest changes without writing
  --help      show this help

With --all, the score path is optional; run the command from the project folder.

### check
cicada check [score.cicada]

validate one score or the current project

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### fmt
cicada fmt [--check|-w] [score.cicada]

format a score or current project

Flags:
  --check     report formatting changes without writing
  -w          write formatted source
  --help      show this help

### play
cicada play [score.cicada] [--audio tymbal|oto|null]

play and watch a score

Flags:
  --audio <name>  select tymbal, oto, or null
  --help          show this help

CICADA_AUDIO selects the backend when --audio is omitted. Tymbal is the default on Windows and Linux; oto is the macOS default. Use --audio oto to select oto explicitly.

### studio
cicada studio [score.cicada] [--listen 127.0.0.1:port] [--audio tymbal|oto|null] [--lsp-stdio]

open the local workstation

Flags:
  --listen <addr>  loopback address; default 127.0.0.1:0
  --audio <name>   select tymbal, oto, or null
  --lsp-stdio      serve LSP on stdin/stdout and Studio on stderr
  --help           show this help

CICADA_AUDIO selects the backend when --audio is omitted. Tymbal is the default on Windows and Linux; oto is the macOS default. Use --audio oto to select oto explicitly.

### lsp
cicada lsp

run the editor language server

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### fields
cicada fields

print the project field catalog as JSON

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### params
cicada params

print the parameter catalog as JSON

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### view
cicada view <score.cicada|project.json> -o <view.html>

write a score or project view as HTML

Flags:
  -o <file>   required output HTML path
  --help      show this help

### explain
cicada explain <construct[.field]> [--json]
cicada explain <score.cicada> <path> [@bar[.beat[.step]]]

explain a language item or parameter value

Flags:
  --json      print construct details as JSON
  --help      show this help

Score locations use bar numbers starting at 1.

### gen
cicada gen [flags]

generate a deterministic phrase

Flags:
  --seed <n>             64-bit generator seed (default 0)
  --key <pitch-class>    tonic pitch class (default c)
  --scale <name>         scale (default minor)
  --root-octave <n>      root octave (default 2)
  --steps <n>            steps per bar (default 16)
  --density <n>          onset density (default 0.6)
  --accent-density <n>   accent density (default 0.5)
  --slide-density <n>    slide density (default 0.4)
  --octave-jump <n>      octave-jump density (default 0.3)
  --swing <percent>      swing percent (default 54)
  --gate <percent>       gate percent (default 55)
  --structure <name>     A, AABA, ABAB, ABAC, or AAAB (default aaba)
  --rest-downbeat        allow a downbeat rest
  --trace                write the draw trace as JSON to stdout
  -o <file>              write the score instead of stdout
  --help                 show this help

### convert
cicada convert <in.cicada|in.json> -o <out.json|out.cicada>

convert source and semantic JSON

Flags:
  -o <file>   required output path with matching extension
  --help      show this help

### compare
cicada compare --semantic <a> <b>

compare two projects

Flags:
  --semantic  compare compiled project meaning
  --help      show this help

### highlight
cicada highlight [--html|--spans] <score.cicada>

print source with syntax highlighting

Flags:
  --html    write HTML highlighting
  --spans   write JSON highlighting spans
  --help    show this help

### symbols
cicada symbols [--refs] [--json] <score.cicada>

list source definitions and references

Flags:
  --refs   include references as well as definitions
  --json   write the symbol list as JSON
  --help   show this help

### render
cicada render <score.cicada> -o <out.wav> [flags]

render a score to WAV

Flags:
  -o <file>                    required output WAV path
  --rate <Hz>                  sample rate (default 48000)
  --bits <16|24|32>            WAV bit depth (default 24)
  --from <bar>                 one-based start bar (default 1)
  --bars <n>                   bars to render; 0 means through song end
  --tail <duration>            render tail (default 3s)
  --dither=<bool>              deterministic TPDF dither for integer PCM (default true)
  --normalize=<bool>           peak normalize to -1 dBFS (default false)
  --block <frames>             offline block size (default 4096)
  --loudness <LUFS>            target integrated loudness
  --true-peak-max <dBTP>       maximum true peak for loudness rendering (default -1)
  --loudness-tolerance <LU>    target tolerance (default 0.5)
  --sampler-baseline           compare one recorded layer/take and 2 ms release
  --export <name>              use a named export profile
  --help                       show this help

Use --from 1 for the first bar. The legacy value --from 0 is accepted with a warning and means bar 1.

### stems
cicada stems <score.cicada> -o <directory> [flags]

render separate float32 WAV stems

Flags:
  -o <directory>           required output directory
  --rate <Hz>              sample rate (default 48000)
  --bits 32                float32 output only
  --from <bar>             one-based start bar (default 1)
  --bars <n>               bars to render; 0 means through song end
  --tail <duration>        render tail (default 3s)
  --dither=<bool>          deterministic TPDF dither option
  --normalize=<bool>       peak normalization option
  --block <frames>         offline block size (default 4096)
  --help                   show this help

Use --from 1 for the first bar. The legacy value --from 0 is accepted with a warning and means bar 1.

### verify-wav
cicada verify-wav <file.wav> [flags]

verify WAV samples and timing

Flags:
  --rate <Hz>                 expected sample rate (default 48000)
  --bits <16|24|32>           expected bit depth (default 24)
  --from <bar>                one-based start bar (default 1)
  --bars <n>                  expected bars (required)
  --tail <duration>           expected tail (default 3s)
  --peak-max-db <dBFS>        peak ceiling (default -0.3)
  --dc-max-db <dBFS>          DC ceiling (default -60)
  --lufs <LUFS>               integrated-loudness target
  --lufs-tolerance <LU>       loudness tolerance (default 0.5)
  --true-peak-max <dBTP>      true-peak ceiling
  --report                    write JSON report to stderr
  --help                      show this help

Use --from 1 for the first bar. The legacy value --from 0 is accepted with a warning and means bar 1.

### verify-stems
cicada verify-stems <directory> [flags]

verify a stem directory

Flags:
  --tap <name>             verification tap (default pre-comp)
  --residual-max-db <dBFS> maximum bus-sum residual (default -80)
  --help                   show this help

### midi
cicada midi <score.cicada> [flags]

export a Standard MIDI File

Flags:
  -o <file>       required output MIDI path
  --bars <n>      song bars; 0 means all (default 0)
  --pattern <id>  export only one pattern
  --report        write JSON report to stderr
  --help          show this help

### verify-midi
cicada verify-midi <file.mid> [flags]

verify a Standard MIDI File

Flags:
  --ppq <n>     expected pulses per quarter note (default 960)
  --type <n>    expected SMF type (default 1)
  --report      write JSON report to stderr
  --help        show this help

### compare-midi
cicada compare-midi <a.mid> <b.mid>

compare MIDI event streams

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### import-midi
cicada import-midi

show MIDI import status

Flags:
  (MIDI import is scheduled; no flags are available)
  --help      show this help

### golden
cicada golden [flags]

check the reference render fingerprint

Flags:
  --update       write the golden fingerprint
  --score <file> score to render (default examples/first-acid.cicada)
  --out <file>   fingerprint path (default testdata/golden/first-acid.fp)
  --rate <Hz>    sample rate (default 48000)
  --bars <n>     bars to render (default 8)
  --help         show this help

